---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import {
  PRODUCT_NAME,
  V1_LINE,
  V2_LINE,
  VENDOR,
  COMPANY_KVK,
  SOURCE_PUBLICATION,
  LICENSING_TERMS_URL,
  COMMERCIAL_EMAIL,
} from '../data/product-facts.mjs';

// The effective date and the "Version YYYY-MM[-DD]" literal in the
// markup below must stay in lockstep with TERMS_VERSION_WEB in
// src/pages/pricing.astro (the pricing page's terms stamp) —
// test/sync/terms-version-sync.test.ts guards it.
const PRODUCT = `${PRODUCT_NAME}`;
const LICENSE = SOURCE_PUBLICATION.license;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of service — mod_pagespeed"
  description={`Terms for modpagespeed.com, the package repositories and support subscriptions; the software is licensed under the ${LICENSE}. Run by ${VENDOR}`}
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-text-body">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-text-annotation">
      Effective date: 20 October 2026 &middot; Version 2026-10-20
    </p>
    <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-text-muted">
      These terms are written in plain language. If something is unclear, email
      <a
        href="mailto:info@we-amp.com"
        class="text-interactive hover:text-interactive-hover underline"
      >
        info@we-amp.com
      </a>{' '}
      and we will clarify.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-12 space-y-10">
      <!-- Scope -->
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-body">What these terms cover</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">
          {VENDOR}, a company registered in the Netherlands (KvK
          <span class="font-mono">{COMPANY_KVK}</span>) and based in Castricum, operates
          modpagespeed.com and the services around {PRODUCT} and its predecessor lines. These terms
          govern your use of:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc list-inside text-text-muted space-y-1">
          <li>the websites we operate for the product, and the tools on them;</li>
          <li>
            the free standard package repository at
            <code class="font-mono text-sm">packages.modpagespeed.com</code>;
          </li>
          <li>
            the private package repository for Priority and Enterprise subscribers, once it is live
            (it is being set up); and
          </li>
          <li>support subscriptions.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
          They apply from the moment you use one of these services. If you use them on behalf of a
          company or other organization, you confirm that you are authorized to bind it, and
          &ldquo;you&rdquo; means that organization. These terms do not govern the software itself
          &mdash; the next section explains what does.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Software license -->
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-body">The software license</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">
          The software &mdash; {PRODUCT}, and the predecessor lines mod_pagespeed {V1_LINE} and
          ModPageSpeed
          {V2_LINE} &mdash; is licensed under the {LICENSE}. That license, not these terms, governs
          your rights to install, run, copy, modify and redistribute the software. It applies to
          every artifact we publish: an artifact you obtain through a subscription carries the same
          license as a standard package.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
          Nothing in these terms narrows the rights the {LICENSE} grants you. Where these terms and
          that license appear to conflict about the software, the license prevails. The license text
          is on the
          <a href="/license/" class="text-interactive hover:text-interactive-hover underline">
            license page
          </a>{' '}
          and ships with every package. Third-party components inside the software remain under
          their own licenses, listed in the packages.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
          mod_pagespeed is an open-source project originally developed at Google. {PRODUCT} is
          developed by {VENDOR} and is not affiliated with or endorsed by Google.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Free standard channel -->
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-body">The free standard packages</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">
          The standard signed packages at
          <code class="font-mono text-sm">packages.modpagespeed.com</code> are free of charge for
          everyone, for any number of servers, in development and in production. The repository is
          public: no account is needed and none is offered, and we do not ask you to register before
          you install. Every package is signed so you can verify what you install.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
          We run the standard repository on a best-effort basis. We aim to keep it available and to
          keep its packages current, but we do not promise uptime, a release schedule, or continued
          publication of any particular package, and we may reorganize the repository with
          reasonable notice on this site. The software in it comes with the warranty terms of the{' '}
          {LICENSE}
          &mdash; that is, as-is, without warranty &mdash; and these terms add none.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Subscriptions -->
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-body">Subscriptions</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">
          We sell support subscriptions, in three tiers: Standard, Priority and Enterprise. Support
          comes from the people who build the product: a direct channel, first-response targets for
          configuration, upgrade and incident questions, and advance notice of security releases.
          What each tier includes, its price and its first-response target are published on the
          <a href="/support/" class="text-interactive hover:text-interactive-hover underline">
            support
          </a>{' '}
          and
          <a href="/pricing/" class="text-interactive hover:text-interactive-hover underline">
            pricing
          </a>{' '}
          pages; the scope and contact channel of your subscription are set out in your order.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
          Everything we sign and attest is the same for every user, with or without a subscription:
          the apt and yum repositories are GPG-signed, release assets are listed with their
          checksums in a SHA256SUMS file, an SPDX software bill of materials (SBOM) is published in
          the source tree, and the container images on GHCR are signed with keyless cosign and carry
          SBOM and build-provenance attestations. A private package repository for Priority and
          Enterprise subscribers is being set up; it is not delivered yet.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">
          <strong>What a subscription grants.</strong> For its term, a subscription gives you the
          support services of your tier and your order. Once the private package repository is live,
          a Priority or Enterprise subscription also gives you access to it. That access is for your
          organization: do not share it outside your organization or use it to mirror the repository
          for others. You may deploy the packages you obtain on as many of your own systems as you
          like, and you may redistribute them under the {LICENSE} &mdash; the restriction is on
          access to the repository, not on the artifacts.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
          <strong>What a subscription does not do.</strong> A subscription covers support and, for
          Priority and Enterprise once it is live, access to the private package repository. The
          software itself is the same for everyone and behaves the same with or without one. A
          subscription grants no rights in the software beyond the {LICENSE}, and it does not make
          us responsible for your deployment (see
          <em>Your responsibilities</em>).
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
          <strong>Ordering and payment.</strong> Prices are published on the
          <a href="/pricing/" class="text-interactive hover:text-interactive-hover underline">
            pricing page
          </a>
          . Standard and Priority subscriptions are bought at checkout from FastSpring, the merchant
          of record; FastSpring processes the payment, and its terms govern the payment and refunds.
          Enterprise subscriptions are invoiced by {VENDOR} directly.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
          <strong>VAT.</strong> Prices exclude VAT. At checkout, FastSpring charges the VAT that
          applies to you; a business in the EU can enter its VAT number there. On an invoice from
          {VENDOR}: customers in the Netherlands are charged 21% BTW; for business customers
          elsewhere in the EU with a valid VAT number, VAT is reverse charged (&ldquo;BTW
          verlegd&rdquo;, Art. 6 Wet OB 1968 / Art. 44 Directive 2006/112/EC); for business
          customers outside the EU, including the United Kingdom, the service is outside the scope
          of Dutch VAT.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
          <strong>Term, renewal and cancellation.</strong> Subscriptions run for one year and renew
          automatically each year unless you cancel before the renewal date. For a subscription
          bought at checkout, FastSpring emails you a reminder one month before the renewal date.
          You can cancel at any time; cancellation takes effect at the end of the current term (for
          consumers, see below). Apart from refunds under FastSpring&rsquo;s terms for a checkout
          purchase and those mandatory law requires, fees already paid are not refunded, except for
          the pro-rata refunds described under <em>Circumstances beyond our control</em> and
          <em>Changes to these terms</em>. Where your order or a subscription agreement states
          something different from these terms, the order or agreement prevails for that
          subscription; the
          <a
            href={LICENSING_TERMS_URL}
            class="text-interactive hover:text-interactive-hover underline"
          >
            We-Amp support terms
          </a>{' '}
          apply alongside these terms.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
          <strong>Consumers (EU/EEA).</strong> If you are a consumer, you have a 14-day right of
          withdrawal under Directive 2011/83/EU; for a subscription bought at checkout you exercise
          it with FastSpring, the seller. If you asked for the subscription to start within those 14
          days and then withdraw, you pay only for the support provided until you withdraw. Once a
          subscription has renewed automatically, you may cancel it at any time with one
          month&rsquo;s notice (Article 6:236(j) of the Dutch Civil Code); it then ends one month
          after your notice, and the fees paid for the period after that date are refunded pro rata.
          Your mandatory statutory rights are unaffected.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
          <strong>Ending a subscription.</strong> We may suspend or end a subscription if you
          materially breach these terms and do not remedy the breach within 14 days of our written
          notice; sharing private package repository access outside your organization ends it
          immediately. When a subscription ends, for whatever reason, support and any access to the
          private package repository end with it. Your right to keep using, modifying and
          redistributing every artifact you already obtained does not end: those artifacts are
          licensed under the {LICENSE}, and nothing we do under these terms revokes that license.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Acceptable use -->
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-body">Acceptable use of the services</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">
          When using our websites, tools and repositories, you may not:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc list-inside text-text-muted space-y-1">
          <li>
            overload, load-test, scrape or benchmark our websites, demo tools or repositories
            without our written permission;
          </li>
          <li>
            circumvent access controls on the private package repository, or share its access
            details outside your organization;
          </li>
          <li>submit sites you have no right to test to the analysis tools on this site;</li>
          <li>use the services to attack, disrupt or overload third-party systems; or</li>
          <li>misrepresent the origin or attestation of a build.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
          These rules are about the services. They do not restrict what you do with the software,
          which is governed by the {LICENSE}.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Your responsibilities -->
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-body">Your responsibilities</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">
          The software runs inline in your web stack and rewrites your live HTTP responses. Before
          you deploy it to production &mdash; and before you deploy any new version, configuration
          change or filter to production &mdash; you agree to:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc list-inside text-text-muted space-y-1">
          <li>
            <strong>Test it first</strong> in a staging or non-production environment that mirrors
            your production setup, and confirm it behaves as you expect.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Keep your own backups</strong> and a tested <strong>rollback plan</strong>, so
            you can disable the software or revert your configuration quickly.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Configure the software correctly</strong> for your environment and keep it
            reasonably up to date.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
          You are responsible for your server configuration, your content and your deployment
          decisions. Roll out gradually &mdash; for example, to a subset of traffic &mdash; and
          monitor before a full rollout. Loss that results from deploying without testing, from
          misconfiguration, or from missing backups or a rollback plan is attributable to you and
          reduces our liability accordingly.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Warranty and liability -->
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-body">Warranty and liability</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">
          <strong>The software.</strong> The software is provided under the {LICENSE} on an
          &ldquo;as is&rdquo; basis, without warranties or conditions of any kind. The license says
          so, and these terms add no warranty on top of it.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
          <strong>The services.</strong> We perform support with reasonable skill and care, and we
          aim to respond within your tier&rsquo;s first-response targets. We do not warrant that
          support will resolve every issue, or that any artifact we publish is free of defects or
          vulnerabilities: signatures, checksums, SBOMs and attestations describe where an artifact
          came from and what went into it, not that it is defect-free. The free services are
          provided as-is.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
          The rest of this section applies to business customers. If you are a consumer in the
          EU/EEA, see <em>Consumers</em> at the end of this section &mdash; these limits do not take
          away your statutory rights.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
          <strong>We are not liable for indirect or consequential loss.</strong> This includes lost
          profits, lost revenue, lost or corrupted data, business interruption, loss of goodwill,
          and claims made against you by third parties &mdash; whether or not we were told such loss
          was possible.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
          <strong>Cap on our liability.</strong> For all other loss, our total liability to you in
          connection with these terms, for all claims combined, is limited to the greater of (a) the
          total fees you paid us in the 12 months immediately before the first event giving rise to
          a claim, or (b) &euro;500. This is an aggregate cap across all claims, not a cap per
          claim. It applies regardless of the legal basis of the claim &mdash; contract, tort (
          <em>onrechtmatige daad</em>), statute or otherwise.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
          <strong>Time limit for claims.</strong> You must tell us about a claim in writing within
          30 days of discovering the issue, and in any event within 12 months of the event that
          caused it. After that, the claim lapses.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
          <strong>What we never limit or exclude.</strong> Nothing in these terms limits or excludes
          our liability for fraud; for intent (<em>opzet</em>) or deliberate recklessness (
          <em>bewuste roekeloosheid</em>) of {VENDOR} or of the persons charged with its management
          or direction; for death or personal injury caused by our negligence; or for anything else
          that cannot be limited or excluded under applicable law.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">
          <strong>Consumers (EU/EEA).</strong> If you are a consumer, nothing in this section
          reduces your mandatory statutory rights, including your legal warranty rights for digital
          content and services and your 14-day right of withdrawal. None of the limits in this
          section applies to you to the extent it would conflict with those rights.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Force majeure -->
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-body">Circumstances beyond our control</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">
          We are not responsible for a failure or delay in operating our websites, repositories or
          support when it is caused by events beyond our reasonable control &mdash; for example,
          outages at our hosting, network or payment providers, internet or infrastructure failures,
          security incidents, natural events, or government action. While such circumstances
          continue, our affected obligations are suspended rather than breached. If they continue
          for more than 60 days, either you or we may end an affected subscription, and we will
          refund any fees you have paid for the unused period.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Data -->
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-body">Data</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">
          The software runs on your servers, sends nothing to us, and never processes your
          visitors&rsquo; data on our behalf. What our websites and services do with personal data,
          and what the software does and does not send, is described in our
          <a
            href="https://we-amp.com/privacy/"
            class="text-interactive hover:text-interactive-hover underline"
          >
            privacy notice
          </a>
          .
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Changes -->
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-body">Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">
          We may update these terms as the product, the law or our processes change. Changes that
          affect a subscription are announced to subscribers by email at least 30 days before they
          take effect; if you do not agree, you may cancel before that date and we will refund any
          prepaid fees for the remaining term. Changes to the terms for the free services take
          effect when published here. The version and date at the top of this page are updated with
          every change.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Governing law -->
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-body">Governing law and venue</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">
          These terms are governed by the laws of the Netherlands. Disputes arising from these terms
          or from your use of the services are submitted to the competent court in Amsterdam, the
          Netherlands. If you are a consumer, you keep the right to bring a claim before the court
          that the law designates for you.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Severability and survival -->
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-body">Severability and survival</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">
          If a provision of these terms (or part of one) is found invalid or unenforceable, it is
          reduced to the minimum extent needed to make it enforceable or, if it cannot be, severed;
          the remaining provisions stay in full force. <em>The software license</em>,
          <em>Warranty and liability</em>, <em>Acceptable use of the services</em> and
          <em>Governing law and venue</em> continue to apply after a subscription or these terms
          end.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Contact -->
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-body">Contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">
          Questions about these terms or about a subscription go to
          <a
            href={`mailto:${COMMERCIAL_EMAIL}`}
            class="text-interactive hover:text-interactive-hover underline"
          >
            {COMMERCIAL_EMAIL}
          </a>
          .
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
